title: The presidential election
subtitle: Hindenburg, Hitler, and a Communist candidate.
new-page: true
tags: kpd_event
view-if: year = 1932 and month >= 2 and civil_war = 0 and y32_president_done = 0
on-arrival: y32_president_done = 1

= Hindenburg or Hitler

Hindenburg's term ends in 1932. The aged Field Marshal, himself a monarchist, is now the only candidate the SPD, the trade unions and the Centre can put up against Hitler, and they put him up. The Nazis, the DNVP's right wing and the Stahlhelm contest with Hitler and Theodor Duesterberg.

The KPD has to choose how to answer. Thälmann can run, as he did in 1925, in the name of the class. The SPD's voters will not vote for him, and many will stay with the old general as the lesser evil.

- @thaelmann: Run Ernst Thälmann.
- @joint: First propose a single left candidate to the SPD and the unions. Run Thälmann when they refuse.

@thaelmann
subtitle: Workers +1. Moscow trust +3.
on-arrival: comintern_trust += 3; workers_kpd += 1*campaign_mult
go-to: y32_president.result

The party runs Thälmann under the slogan "A vote for Hindenburg is a vote for Hitler, a vote for Thälmann is a vote against Hitler". The first half of the slogan is wrong and everyone knows it, since Hindenburg is the one candidate who can keep Hitler out. The second half would be an argument if the vote were not split.

@joint
subtitle: Unity +1, workers +1. Moscow trust -5.
