On 13 March Hindenburg receives 49.5 per cent, Hitler 30.1, Thälmann 13.2 and Duesterberg 6.8. In the runoff on 10 April Hindenburg wins with 53.1 per cent, Hitler has 36.8 and Thälmann 10.2. The Republic is saved, by an old man who despises it, and with the votes of the party that is hated in the barracks and at the Stahlhelm.

Within two months he will dismiss the Chancellor who was elected with those votes.

- @root: Continue.
